# PR evidence convention

When shipping a fix or feature via a pull request for this repo:

1. Put visual proof in the **PR description**, one change per bullet:
   - `Fixed …` / `Added …` followed by a screenshot and/or short recording
2. Store media under `docs/pr-evidence/` when practical; link raw GitHub URLs so they render in the PR
3. End the **user-facing chat reply** with:

```
Updated PR #<n>, preview <preview-url>.
PR includes screenshots and recordings showing the fix/feature.
```

Skip the trailing block only if no PR was created or updated in that turn.
